      meta: "Emails · 2 min read",
      body: `<h4>Purpose</h4><p>Follow this SOP to complete use reminder vs escalate templates from issue actions in a consistent and auditable way.</p><h4>Prerequisites</h4><ul><li>Open issue email action panel in the portal.</li><li>Keep relevant invoice, customer, or issue reference ready.</li><li>Confirm your role has update permission for this action.</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Open <strong>issue email action panel</strong> and locate the target record.</li><li>Use search and filters to narrow to the correct invoice, issue, customer, or task.</li><li>Perform the action for <em>use reminder vs escalate templates from issue actions</em> and add required remarks.</li><li>Save or submit using the available workflow button.</li><li>Review post-action status, trail entries, and dependent module updates.</li></ol><h4>Validation</h4><ul><li>Status and sub-status are updated as expected.</li><li>Action trail captures user, timestamp, and remark.</li><li>Linked dashboards, notifications, or task queues show the latest state.</li></ul><h4>Common issues</h4><ul><li>Submitting without validating current status and ownership.</li><li>Forgetting mandatory remark or recipient details.</li><li>Assuming save was successful without checking trail or counters.</li></ul>`
