      id: "kb-139", cat: "dashboards",
      title: "How to show invoices with unread emails",
      meta: "Dashboards · 2 min read",
      roles: ["Agent"],
      body: `<h4>Purpose</h4><p>Narrow the All Customers invoice list to invoices with unread email activity.</p><h4>Prerequisites</h4><ul><li>Sign in with an Agent account.</li><li>Open All Customers.</li></ul><h4>Steps</h4><ol><li>Locate Unread Emails above the invoice table.</li><li>Click Unread Emails to turn the filter on.</li><li>Review the remaining invoice rows and verify the invoice and customer before opening one.</li><li>Click Unread Emails again to turn the filter off.</li></ol><p><strong>Important note:</strong> The unread badge counts unread emails. Other active invoice filters and searches still apply while Unread Emails is on.</p><h4>Validation</h4><ul><li>The toggle shows its active state when enabled.</li><li>Only invoices with an unread email count remain in the filtered list.</li><li>Turning it off removes the unread-only restriction.</li></ul><h4>Common issues</h4><ul><li>Assuming the badge is the number of invoices.</li><li>Overlooking another active filter when an expected invoice is absent.</li><li>Taking action without verifying the invoice number and customer.</li></ul>`
